  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>This family campsite in Grimaud, right in the heart of the Gulf of Saint-Tropez, welcomes dogs with a genuine gesture: a small gift (poop bags, bowl, toy) is waiting for the dog on arrival.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you book</h2>
      <p>The campsite accepts up to two dogs per pitch, with a 40kg weight limit each, and excludes category 1 and 2 dogs — rules confirmed by two independent, consistent sources (emmenetonchien.com and tourisme-avec-mon-chien.com). The exact dog supplement for this specific establishment could not be confirmed (not to be confused with the different rates of other campsites in the same Tikayan chain): ask for the amount directly when booking. An outdoor pool (open from early April to late September), shaded green areas and pétanque courts are available during your stay, over a season that generally runs from April to early November.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: the Figuière wine estate in La Londe-les-Maures offers 100% dog-friendly tours and tastings, a nice outing from the campsite.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Several dog-friendly beaches on the Gulf of Saint-Tropez are a few minutes' drive from the campsite.</p>
